        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain replace-mode filtering in model picker",
        "body": "Closes #104545\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users with `models.mode: \"replace\"` would see only explicitly configured models in the Control UI without any explanation, making newly bundled or discovered models appear unsupported.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing replace-mode filtering remains unchanged. Configured model-list responses now carry additive `catalogMode: \"replace\"` metadata, and the chat model picker plus Quick Settings use it to show a localized explanation with a direct \"Manage models\" action. Full-catalog (`view: \"all\"`) responses do not carry the hint metadata.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can immediately tell that their local replace-mode configuration is filtering the catalog and can open model settings to add models or change the catalog mode, instead of debugging upstream model support.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head refresh: rebased onto `main` at `17630226fc`; pushed head `f414fbb2547`.\n- Focused Gateway and UI regressions: 6 files, 299 tests passed.\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/chat/models.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/config/quick.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/models.test.ts`\n- Browser regression: `ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts`, 7 tests passed with the repository's UI E2E Vitest config.\n- Exact-head deterministic visual proof against a mocked `chat.metadata` replace-mode response:\n  - desktop 1280x900: hint and action visible; menu contained within viewport; no horizontal overflow\n  - mobile 393x852: 369px menu contained within viewport; hint wraps cleanly; no horizontal overflow\n- Focused `oxfmt` and type-aware `oxlint` passed for all touched source and test files.\n- The final diff retains the two new keys only in `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`; non-English bundles and `.i18n` metadata match current `main`. The expected two pending fallback keys remain for authenticated post-merge `control-ui-locale-refresh` handling per `ui/AGENTS.md`.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n\nBefore: the configured model rows were shown with no indication that replace mode hid other catalog entries.\n\nAfter: the picker and Quick Settings state, \"Replace mode shows only models explicitly listed in Settings,\" with a \"Manage models\" action.\n\nCrabbox was unavailable in this checkout, so visual proof used the repository's deterministic Control UI mock gateway and local Chromium fallback. The same repository UI E2E Vitest config was run directly and passed.\n\nExact-head local Codex autoreview was attempted. The configured model requires a newer CLI, and the supported-model fallback was rejected by local approval policy because it would export the unpublished diff/repository context to an external service.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex was used to implement and review this change. No agent transcript is attached.\n",
